1
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:10,350
(Passenger Drop-off Area)

2
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,360
=Vow of Autumn=
=Episode 14=

3
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:41,859
Ma'am,

4
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:43,140
I'm still on duty,

5
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:44,280
so I won't take you home.

6
00:00:44,479 --> 00:00:44,899
Okay.

7
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,259
Thanks for your help,

8
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:47,079
Dr. Pei.

9
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,140
You've been running around for me.

10
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:50,460
I've kept you from work.

11
00:00:50,939 --> 00:00:51,960
Not at all.

12
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,320
When you get home,

13
00:00:53,619 --> 00:00:54,340
get more rest.

14
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:55,240
Take meds on time.

15
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,479
Follow-up next week, okay?

16
00:00:56,479 --> 00:00:57,619
(No Smoking)
I will.

17
00:00:57,899 --> 00:00:58,780
Don't let me keep you.

18
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:29,060
That Dr. Pei

19
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:30,260
is quite sharp

20
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:31,599
and reliable.

21
00:01:32,299 --> 00:01:34,480
Not like other boys his age,

22
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:35,719
all reckless and impatient.

23
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,099
He's a surgeon.

24
00:01:38,159 --> 00:01:39,439
He has to be steady to do surgery.

25
00:01:39,939 --> 00:01:41,140
Good point.

26
00:01:42,959 --> 00:01:45,659
I wonder if surgeons his age

27
00:01:45,659 --> 00:01:46,760
are very busy.

28
00:01:47,719 --> 00:01:49,579
Do you think he has a girlfriend?

29
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:54,019
(Nurse Station)

30
00:01:54,019 --> 00:01:54,600
Qingqing,

31
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:57,379
I think he likes you.

32
00:01:58,079 --> 00:01:58,659
Look,

33
00:01:58,879 --> 00:02:00,780
all this time I've been here,

34
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,620
he's kept coming by.

35
00:02:02,859 --> 00:02:04,719
Says he's checking on me,

36
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:06,920
but he only has eyes for you.

37
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:07,579
Mom.

38
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,120
You know

39
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:10,740
he's Su Mu's brother.

40
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:12,560
He's practically your godson.

41
00:02:12,719 --> 00:02:14,360
And he's 6 years younger than me.

42
00:02:14,479 --> 00:02:16,659
What does age matter?

43
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,740
He's Su Mu's brother,

44
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,280
not yours.

45
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:22,199
As long as you like him.

46
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:23,800
You know,

47
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:26,139
just because your dad and I split up...

48
00:02:26,199 --> 00:02:27,520
Okay, Mom.

49
00:02:27,599 --> 00:02:28,699
Stop worrying about me.

50
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:29,580
Let's go.

51
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:32,460
I just want you to be happy.

52
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,140
(Legal Aid Case Form)

53
00:02:40,141 --> 00:02:41,120
(Case Summary / Claims)

54
00:02:49,639 --> 00:02:50,180
Chen.

55
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,639
Helping me with this legal aid case,

56
00:02:54,919 --> 00:02:56,479
running between the hospital
and the site...

57
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,639
It takes so much time,

58
00:02:57,639 --> 00:02:58,800
but hardly pays.

59
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,080
Feel like you're losing out?

60
00:03:01,219 --> 00:03:02,020
Why would I?

61
00:03:02,659 --> 00:03:03,840
We're still working

62
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:04,780
on other big cases,

63
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:05,979
but we can handle both.

64
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,199
Besides,

65
00:03:07,719 --> 00:03:08,919
I studied law

66
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,360
to help people solve problems.

67
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,419
Using my skills to help that girl...

68
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:14,860
This feels great.

69
00:03:16,819 --> 00:03:17,639
But, Ms. Wen,

70
00:03:18,199 --> 00:03:19,759
you've changed lately.

71
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:21,460
How?

72
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,639
You seem warmer

73
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:24,919
and more alive.

74
00:03:26,659 --> 00:03:28,900
I wonder who's behind that.

75
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,319
(Good night.)

76
00:03:47,759 --> 00:03:49,000
(Whatever happens,)

77
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,120
(good or bad,)

78
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:52,719
(you can tell me.)

79
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,500
(I'll always be here for you.)

80
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:10,680
(Pei Yiqiu
Are you free later? I'd like to...)

81
00:04:14,659 --> 00:04:15,719
(Are you free later?)

82
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:17,079
(About Xiaoyu's case...)

83
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,980
(I'd like to ask you a few things.)

84
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,579
Please put it here.

85
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:39,639
Careful.

86
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:42,579
Ms. Su.

87
00:04:43,459 --> 00:04:44,899
Our partner got back to us.

88
00:04:45,079 --> 00:04:47,000
The deal is confirmed.

89
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,560
Really? It's definite?

90
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:50,920
The paperwork's already started.

91
00:04:51,519 --> 00:04:52,060
Oh,

92
00:04:52,439 --> 00:04:52,920
they said

93
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,660
you probably know their lawyer,

94
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,160
Gu Yuan.

95
00:04:56,399 --> 00:04:57,759
He'll handle the legal side

96
00:04:57,759 --> 00:04:58,800
throughout the project.

97
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:03,139
Okay.

98
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,060
Got it.

99
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:50,959
It's this late already.

100
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,000
What is it?

101
00:05:56,519 --> 00:05:57,800
The partnership.

102
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,339
You deliberately let me know

103
00:06:01,279 --> 00:06:02,660
you were their lawyer.

104
00:06:09,939 --> 00:06:11,620
You just wanted me to come, didn't you?

105
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,639
And that night at the bar,

106
00:06:24,899 --> 00:06:26,639
didn't you want me to see you?

107
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,319
Are you sober?

108
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:44,019
What do you mean?

109
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,860
I don't want you to deny this tomorrow.

110
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,279
I'm perfectly sober.

111
00:07:51,959 --> 00:07:54,560
Quiz me on any divorce provision.

112
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,660
I'll recite it word for word.

113
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,560
Then tell me,

114
00:08:01,279 --> 00:08:03,740
what's Article 1079 of the Civil Code?

115
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,920
A spouse seeking divorce

116
00:08:07,519 --> 00:08:09,600
may seek mediation by a relevant body

117
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:11,379
or file directly

118
00:08:11,379 --> 00:08:12,519
with a people's court.

119
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,160
In divorce cases, the court

120
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:16,439
shall attempt mediation.

121
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,439
If the marriage has broken down

122
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,720
and mediation fails,

123
00:08:19,819 --> 00:08:20,920
divorce shall be granted.

124
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,500
Do I get a prize if I'm right?

125
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:18,880
(Passenger Drop-off Area)
